message: "Cite this exact archived version 1.4.0 for retained results and conditional residual-six proofs; the original Boolean existence problem remains open."
type: "software"
title: "Exact spectral exclusions, singleton components, graph locality and residual-six lemmas for degree-five Boolean candidates"
version: "1.4.0"
authors: [{"family-names": "Towell", "given-names": "Alexander Richard", "orcid": "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-6443-9897", "affiliation": "Southern Illinois University Edwardsville"}]
license: ["MIT", "CC-BY-4.0"]
abstract: "Written tripled-quartic, private-tip, three-free classification, endpoint, common-core and disk arguments give a conditional negative-quintic support-union bound of 12 at residual defect at most 6. Inherited derivative and normalization premises remain explicit; the whole Boolean-pattern application has further unbundled graph premises. Standard-library controls corroborate the mechanisms, without constructing a Boolean function. Substantial AI assistance is disclosed; the global problem remains open. No novelty, formal verification or human peer review is established."
